.TH "UNICODE\-TAG\-STDIN" "1" "January 2020" "secure-terminal" "secure-terminal Manual"
.SH "NAME"
\fBunicode\-tag\-stdin\fR \- stdin\-only unicode\-tag for confined use
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBunicode\-tag\-stdin\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
unicode\-tag\-stdin is \fBunicode\-tag\fR(1) restricted to standard input: it reads no files and takes no path arguments, so it can run under a tight AppArmor profile (named \fBunicode\-tag\-stdin\fR) that denies all data\-file access\. It is the tool the tool\-output neutralizer pipes untrusted text through\. The tagging is identical to \fBunicode\-tag\fR(1)\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Read a JSON request \fB{"unicode\-tag\-json": VALUE}\fR and write \fB{"unicode\-tag\-json\-result": TAGGED}\fR, where every string in VALUE (object keys and values, at any depth) is tagged\. One process tags a whole document, instead of one process per string\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success; 1 on an unreadable standard input, a malformed \fB\-\-json\fR request, or a closed output pipe\.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBunicode\-tag\fR(1)
